# Proteus — per-archon ignore rules.
#
# Every Archon carries its own .gitignore so the state/ vs out/ split holds wherever
# the archon is checked out, not just inside this repo's tree (whose root .gitignore also
# covers archons/*/out|state as a safety net). See seneschal/references/archons.md.

# --- state/ : runtime churn — rewritten every cycle, regenerable, never in git ---
# (rolling ledgers, "latest" caches, counters, queues, sentinels, pid/log files)
state/*
!state/README.md
!state/*.example.json
!state/*.example.jsonl
!state/*.example.md

# --- out/ : deliverables — drafted documents, digests, generated views ----------
# Products, not machinery. Ignored here because Proteus's outputs embed the owner's
# contact details (tailored resumes/cover letters); the generator is tracked, its
# output isn't.
out/

# --- secrets: only the *.example is ever tracked --------------------------------
*.env
!*.env.example
*.secret
*_token.json

# --- private inputs: only the *.example is ever tracked -------------------------
profile.json
watchlist.json
voice-profile.md

# --- local noise ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
*.pid
*.stackdump
